{"base_rate":0.13561847988077497,"brier":0.077526825633383,"bss":0.3386556366047747,"bss_hi":0.4398703269599798,"bss_lo":0.20573100987557708,"chart":{"base":[237.9,58.7],"fp":[227.1,316.6],"lead":"62,258.9 272,234.3 482,187.4 692,122.9","note":{"base":"skill 0.34 — higher than 64% of cities","fp":"low end +3pp, high end +12pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.0 °C — better than 63% of cities","rel":"promised 0% → rained 4%; promised 55% → rained 47%"},"rel":"62,448.9 102.1,437.8 410.2,260.9"},"country":"MA","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.03891207153502233,"ess":234.16008754329098,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Marrakesh</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Marrakesh rain forecast is moderately skilful, though 2 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (79%), believe about\n<b>66%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>4%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 671 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-03-26. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 4.6 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.34, ranked 77 of\n213 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(40&ndash;144) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>4%</b></td><td class='num'>379</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>3%</td><td class='num'><b>3%</b></td><td class='num'>67</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>9%</td><td class='num'><b>9%</b></td><td class='num'>86</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>31%</td><td class='num'><b>29%</b></td><td class='num'>69</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>79%</td><td class='num'><b>66%</b></td><td class='num'>70</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">2 of 5 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Marrakesh</b> <span class=\"muted\">Morocco</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag ok\">Moderately skilful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">2 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.34</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>40&ndash;144\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 213</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>671 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Marrakesh &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Marrakesh\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\