42.8\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 4% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 379 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.0\" cy=\"367.5936675461741\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 3%&amp;#10;It rained 3% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 67 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"68.62\" cy=\"371.13432835820896\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 9%&amp;#10;It rained 9% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 86 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"89.77767441860465\" cy=\"348.13953488372096\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 31%&amp;#10;It rained 29% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 69 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"167.89391304347825\" cy=\"276.4927536231884\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 79%&amp;#10;It rained 66% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 70 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"338.1657142857142\" cy=\"142.8\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(14%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Marrakesh the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (0.34) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (-0.21).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>1%</td><td class='num'>-0.213</td><td class='num'>1.9%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>7%</td><td class='num'>0.070</td><td class='num'>4.1%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>174</td><td class='num'>32%</td><td class='num'>0.289</td><td class='num'>11.8%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>137</td><td class='num'>15%</td><td class='num'>0.345</td><td class='num'>5.3%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":31.63416,"lon":-7.99994,"n":671,"n_cities":213,"name":"Marrakesh","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.03,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0,"n":379,"obs":0.0395778364116095,"sig":true},{"hi":0.05,"lo":0.03,"mean":0.029999999999999995,"n":67,"obs":0.029850746268656716,"sig":false},{"hi":0.18,"lo":0.05,"mean":0.08976744186046512,"n":86,"obs":0.09302325581395349,"sig":false},{"hi":0.55,"lo":0.18,"mean":0.3104347826086956,"n":69,"obs":0.2898550724637681,"sig":false},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.55,"mean":0.7914285714285713,"n":70,"obs":0.6571428571428571,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":4.6,"provisional":false,"rank":77,"rank_hi":144.04999999999995,"rank_lo":40.0,"reliability":0.0028108637396571396,"resolution":0.03737994976739098,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"marrakesh","station":"","timezone":"Africa/Casablanca"}